  "verbalization": "Aripiprazole is implicated in the pathogenesis of several adverse effects through a shared mechanism involving Paliperidone, both of which bind to Adra2c. The evidence suggests that Aripiprazole causes adverse effects such as oropharyngeal spasm, electrocardiogram t-wave abnormalities, and eye movement disorders, all of which are mediated by Paliperidone. These effects are linked to Adra2c through the binding of Paliperidone to the receptor, indicating a potential role for Adra2c in the pathophysiology of these conditions. The commonality in the pathways highlights a possible overlap in the mechanisms by which Aripiprazole and Paliperidone influence Adra2c, suggesting that the receptor may be a key target in the context of these adverse effects. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Aripiprazole and Paliperidone share a common pathway involving Adra2c, underscoring the importance of this receptor in the adverse effects associated with these drugs.",
